``` DET-025 - Kerberoasting (T1558.003)
``` Two complementary rules + one correlation signal. Built by Claude over Splunk MCP, 2026-10-31
``` (Eval 06), inspecting real 4769 data first. Validated against the 11:17 test (bob.user -> svc_sql, RC4).
```
``` Context: this detection was built to close a gap the local RAG analyst flagged ("no Kerberoasting
``` coverage"). Requires "Audit Kerberos Service Ticket Operations" enabled on the DC (4769).
```
``` Data-pipeline note: IpAddress is extracted TWICE in win_dc (duplicate multivalue), so a plain
``` replace() returns null and `by src_ip` silently drops events. Use mvindex(IpAddress,0). Worth fixing
``` at props.conf (same duplicate-extraction issue seen in the brute-force detection).
``` Baseline note: 4769 auditing was only just enabled, so normal machine-account 4769s had not yet
``` accumulated. Let benign 4769s flow before trusting thresholds; every 4768 in 30 days was AES256.

``` ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
``` Rule 1 - RC4 service ticket for a user SPN account (HIGH fidelity in an all-AES domain)
``` Saved search / report Title: "DET-025a - Kerberoasting RC4 Service Ticket (T1558.003)"
``` Schedule every 5 min, earliest=-10m@m latest=-5m@m (the 5-min lag absorbs forwarder delay).
index=win_dc EventCode=4769 Status=0x0 TicketEncryptionType=0x17
| eval service=lower(ServiceName),
       requester=lower(mvindex(split(TargetUserName,"@"),0)),
       src_ip=replace(mvindex(IpAddress,0),"^::ffff:","")
| where NOT match(service,"\$$") AND service!="krbtgt" AND NOT like(service,"krbtgt/%")
| where NOT match(requester,"\$$")
| fillnull value="unknown" src_ip
| stats min(_time) as firstTime max(_time) as lastTime count
        values(service) as services dc(service) as spn_count
        values(TicketOptions) as ticket_options by requester src_ip
| convert ctime(firstTime) ctime(lastTime)
``` Threshold: 1 event - every ticket in this domain is AES, so one RC4 user-SPN ticket is already abnormal.
``` False positives: legacy/RC4-only service accounts, Java/Linux keytab clients, cross-forest trusts.
``` Fix the account (grant AES) rather than suppress. Blind spot: an attacker requesting AES is invisible here.

``` ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
``` Rule 2 - one account requesting many distinct user SPNs (any encryption) - behavioural backup
``` Saved search / report Title: "DET-025b - Kerberoasting Mass SPN Requests (T1558.003)"
``` Schedule every 10 min, earliest=-20m@m latest=-5m@m, dedupe on requester.
index=win_dc EventCode=4769 Status=0x0
| eval service=lower(ServiceName),
       requester=lower(mvindex(split(TargetUserName,"@"),0)),
       src_ip=replace(mvindex(IpAddress,0),"^::ffff:","")
| where NOT match(service,"\$$") AND service!="krbtgt" AND NOT like(service,"krbtgt/%")
| where NOT match(requester,"\$$")
| bin _time span=10m
| stats dc(service) as distinct_spns count as tickets values(service) as services
        values(TicketEncryptionType) as enc_types values(src_ip) as src_ips by _time requester
| eval rc4_present=if(isnotnull(mvfind(enc_types,"^0x17$")),"yes","no")
| where distinct_spns>=3
``` Threshold: >=3 distinct user SPNs in 10 min (educated guess on a thin baseline - run without the
``` where for 1-2 weeks and set just above the 99th percentile per user). When rc4_present=yes, treat as critical.
``` Catches AES-based and mass roasting Rule 1 can't see. Misses single-target roasts and throttled requests.
``` FPs: admin consoles (SSMS to many SQL instances), monitoring/backup accounts, scanners, SCCM, delegation.

``` ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
``` Correlation signal (cheap third angle): SPN enumeration from a non-admin host seconds before the request.
``` Saved search / report Title: "DET-025c - SPN Enumeration (Kerberoast precursor)"
(index=sysmon EventCode=1) OR (index=windows EventCode=4688)
    (CommandLine="*setspn*" OR CommandLine="*GetUserSPNs*" OR CommandLine="*KerberosRequestorSecurityToken*"
     OR CommandLine="*servicePrincipalName*" OR CommandLine="*Rubeus*")
| eval cmd=coalesce(CommandLine, Process_Command_Line), user=coalesce(User, SubjectUserName)
| table _time index host user cmd ParentImage
| sort _time
``` In the test, `setspn -T lab.local -Q */*` ran on WIN-CL01 ~9 seconds before the RC4 ticket request.
